#   device      edge1050, same digest-pinned container as the green capture
#
# TWO transformations, both stated because neither is invisible:
#   1. the `<job>\t<step>\t<timestamp> ` prefix that `gh run view --log` prepends
#      to every line, removed (as in monkeydo-green-run.log);
#   2. two `set -x` trace lines the JOB's own shell emitted --
#        + echo '----- simulator log -----'
#        + cat /tmp/sim.log
#      -- which the runner interleaved into this region of the job-log stream on
#      this run. They are not monkeydo output and are not in /tmp/ciq-test.log;
#      a file fed to --monkeydo-log must be the monkeydo stream, so they are
#      dropped. The green capture needed no such removal: its region of the
#      stream carries no trace lines.
# Nothing else was edited -- no line reordered, reflowed or re-spaced -- and the
# ERROR row and the FAILED summary are the simulator's own bytes.
#
# WHY A RED FIXTURE IS COMMITTED. The green capture proves the parser accepts a
# real pass. Only a real failing transcript proves it rejects a real failure at
# the bytes the simulator actually emits -- a synthetic FAIL row cannot, because
# the suite's own builder wrote it. This one carries the shape that matters:
# a clean-looking `Ran 17 tests` and sixteen PASS rows, with the failure visible
# only in one ERROR row and in `FAILED (passed=16, failed=0, errors=1)`.
#
